('TV Show', 'The Carol Burnett Show', NULL, 'Carol Burnett, Tim Conway, Vicki Lawrence, Lucille Ball, Harvey Korman, Lyle Waggoner, Ernie Anderson, Steve Lawrence, Dick Van Dyke, Eydie Gorme, Bernadette Peters, Mel Torme, Martha Raye, Cass Elliot, Roddy McDowall, Vincent Price, Jonathan Winters, Carl Reiner, Rock Hudson, Andy Griffith, Betty White, Carol Channing, Soupy Sales, Ruth Buzzi, Joan Rivers, Tom Smothers, Sammy Davis Jr., Cher, Don Rickles, Steve Martin, Burt Reynolds', NULL, NULL, 1972, '13+', '1 Season', 'Comedy', 'For over a decade, this extravaganza of comedy, song and dance defined entertainment for TV viewers. The Carol Burnett Show brought the actors and audience close together. Beloved for her signature audience Questions and Answers famous Tarzan yell, Burnett''s brilliant troupe stars Harvey Korman, Vicki Lawrence and Lyle Waggoner.', 'Prime Video'),
('Movie', 'The Capture', 'John Sturges', 'Lew Ayres, Teresa Wright, Victor Jory, Duncan Renaldo, Jacqueline White', NULL, NULL, 1950, '18+', '102 min', 'Western', 'Lin Vanner (Ayres) captures and turns in a fellow oil company employee whom he believes was behind a payroll robbery. The accused man dies in police custody, and Lin feels overwhelmingly responsible for the man''s death, wondering if he was actually innocent of the crime. His guilt causes Lin to lose his job and his fiancee, and to soothe his conscience, Lin seeks out the dead man''s widow, Evelyn (Wright). The two fall in love and marry without Evelyn ever knowing about Lin''s past and feelings of guilt. When Lin discovers who really commited the robbery, he goes after the man, who dies accidentally in the ensuing chase. Lin is now accused of murdering the man, and must become a fugitive on the run. This is the lost masterpiece of director John Sturges.', 'Prime Video'),
