('Movie', 'Silent Wings - The American Glider Pilots of WWII', 'Robert Child', 'Hal Holbrook, Walter Cronkite, Andy Rooney, Michael J. Samek', NULL, NULL, 2007, '7+', '115 min', 'Documentary, Special Interest', 'From the early race to build gliders to the D-Day invasion at Normandy and Nazi Germany''s final surrender, this acclaimed feature documentary, narrated by Hal Holbrook, reveals the critical role gliders played in World War II offensives. Through rare archival footage and photographs, the film places the audience right at the center of the action in the dangerous world of American glider pilot.', 'Prime Video'),
