('TV Show', 'Julian Fellowes Presents Doctor Thorne', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2016, '13+', '1 Season', 'Drama', 'From the creator of Downton Abbey. Dr. Thorne lives a quiet life with niece Mary in Greshambury, home of the wealthy Gresham family. Unbeknownst to others, the Greshams have lost their fortune and matriarch Lady Arabella has a scheme to regain it via an arranged marriage with her son and an American heiress. However, her son plans to elope with Mary, which complicates Lady Arabella''s plans.', 'Prime Video'),
('TV Show', 'Judith Lucy: Judith Lucy Vs Men', NULL, 'Judith Lucy', NULL, NULL, 2020, '16+', '1 Season', 'Comedy, Talk Show and Variety', 'Judith Lucy is single again. Reflecting on her entire history with men, she concludes that maybe it’s time to shut up shop: ‘Whatever it is that I’m selling, a lot of straight men simply aren’t interested in buying it.’ In this show Jude recounts her full history with the opposite sex and asks the audience to determine whether she should ever date again. Should Judith hang up her vagina for good?', 'Prime Video'),
('Movie', 'Judge Priest', 'John Ford', 'Will Rogers, Anita Louise, Tom Brown, Henry B. Wawlthall, David Landau, Rochelle Hudson, Hattie McDaniel, Stepin Fetchit', NULL, NULL, 1934, 'PG', '81 min', 'Comedy, Drama', 'Small-town Judge William "Billy" Priest (Rogers) in the old south stirs up the place with stinging humor and common-sense observances as he tangles with prejudices and civil injustices. Also, Judge Priest tries to play matchmaker between orphan Ellie May Gillespie (Louise) and his lawyer nephew Jerome Priest (Brown). Funny, warm slice of American 19th century life. One of three collaborations between Will Rogers and John Ford.', 'Prime Video'),
('Movie', 'Joyride', 'Joseph Ruben', 'Robert Carradine, Melanie Griffith', NULL, NULL, 1977, 'R', '92 min', 'Action, Comedy, Documentary', 'Three fun-loving teenagers decide to leave their dull jobs in California and head north to Alaska''a pipeline in search of romance and adventure.', 'Prime Video'),
